    "summary": "JPMorgan Chase operates under multiple account numbers with specific bariatric surgery requirements differentiated by account (3174696 requires PHT CM engagement, 2501770 does not). The account offers a non-standard fertility/infertility benefit with tiered coverage based on WinFertility engagement ($35,000 with WinFertility vs $10,000 without, effective 7.1.24), covering elective cryopreservation without requiring an infertility diagnosis. An Expanded Travel Benefit effective 7.1.22 provides reimbursement for in-network services beyond 50 miles with lifetime maximums of $10,000 for bariatric, transplant, and other medical services (unlimited for behavioral). Effective 8.1.24, case management (except Transplant and Gene Therapy) and customer service for FL, GA, OK, and LA residents are carved out to Included Health (833.938.9874), while Cigna retains UM and YHF Coaching programs. The pharmacy benefit includes a CVS Caremark DBA program requiring 111 self-administered specialty medications to go through CVS for authorization if given subcutaneously."
}